# Snow Leopard compatibility patch 0022
#
# Incompatibility: the 10.6 SDK and runtime have no NSURLSession, secure-coder
# class filters, request service types, automatic termination, or URL cache lookup.
# Behaviour preserved: the complete 1.27.3 downloader contract remains active
# through Sparkle's final NSURLDownload implementation, including redirects,
# HTTPS, progress, response metadata, cancellation, and persistent destinations.
# History: 8a0474d6 introduced the deprecated downloader beside NSURLSession.
# c3c1b1af removed it only when Sparkle raised its minimum from 10.7 to 10.9.
# ecb608bb introduced the coder models. 282f0ae5 added warning-only generics.
# Public API evidence: NSURLDownload, NSCoding, cache path search, and explicit
# decoded-class validation are public on 10.6.
# Safety: the NSURLSession source is explicitly excluded only for the 10.6 SDK.
# Newer SDK builds retain it. Decoded fallback objects are class-checked.
